    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Minn and Mek freeze in place as Nine approaches, their eyes flickering with a mix of suspicion and curiosity. Minn narrows his gaze, sizing up the elf with cool calculation, while Mek shifts restlessly, his tail flicking nervously. Neither speaks at first, exchanging a brief glance as if silently weighing whether Nine is friend or foe. Finally, Minn breaks the silence with a cautious, clipped tone, \u201cYou\u2019re new. What business do you have with Sparkrender\u2019s kin?\u201d Mek\u2019s voice follows, sharper and more impatient, \u201cSpeak quickly. We don\u2019t have time for strangers.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the party never knows information they haven't been told just roleplay the interaction with minn and meek "
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Minn narrows his eyes, voice low and cautious. \u201cWho are you, and why have you come here?\u201d Mek\u2019s tail flicks sharply as he steps forward, hissing, \u201cState your business. This is Sparkrender\u2019s domain. Strangers aren\u2019t welcome.\u201d Their claws scrape softly against the stone beneath their feet as they wait, alert and ready, eyes fixed on the approaching figure."
    },
    {
