    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Minn\u2019s gaze sharpens at Fenwick\u2019s words, a flicker of disbelief crossing his face. \u201cA dragon god, you say?\u201d he scoffs, voice dripping with skepticism. Mek steps closer, tail twitching, and hisses, \u201cDon\u2019t waste our time with lies. We know better than to trust smooth tongues.\u201d Their eyes narrow, unwavering in suspicion as they await the party\u2019s next move, ready to challenge any falsehoods told in their domain."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "only describe the kobolds action and words."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Minn\u2019s gaze sharpens, voice low and icy. \u201cA dragon god? Bold claim. Prove it, or leave.\u201d Mek\u2019s tail flicks with impatience as he steps closer, claws scraping against the stone. \u201cWe\u2019ve heard many lies from trespassers. Spare us your tales unless you have proof.\u201d Their eyes narrow, bodies tense and ready, silently daring the visitors to back their words with deeds."
